{"latest_judgment":{"docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_25_140887620#0_287163141","relevance":3,"reason":"This Mayo Clinic Q&A is directly dedicated to whether lactose intolerance can develop later in life and states that lactose intolerance can develop at any age.","learned":"Mayo Clinic says lactose intolerance can develop at any age and may be triggered by other medical conditions such as Crohn’s disease."},"action":{"op":"next","qid":"q167","reason":"This medical phrasing retrieved a highly authoritative, directly relevant source; continue to find more independent grade-3 evidence."}}
{"request":{"op":"next","qid":"q167"},"response":{"docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_46_154644860#0_359451221","ok":true,"op":"next","qid":"q167","rank":2,"snippet":"{ \"docid\": \"msmarco_v2.1_doc_46_154644860#0_359451221\" , \"end_char\": 1064.000000 , \"headings\": \"Can <cover>Lactose Intolerance Develop with Age?</cover>Can Lactose Intolerance Develop with Age? Symptoms Other Causes Solutions \" , \"segment\": \"Can Lactose Intolerance Develop with Age? Manhattan Gastroenterology Can Lactose Intolerance Develop with Age? Although lactose intolerance usually begins when you’re around age two, it isn’t until you reach adolescence or adulthood that the symptoms typically appear for many people. In fact, the condition is more likely to appear in adults, and the older you get, the more likely it is that you’ll discover you’re lactose intolerant. Lactose intolerance is a condition best described as the inability to process lactose, the sugar found in milk and milk products. To properly digest lactose, you need a sufficient amount of an enzyme called lactase, which is produced in the lining of your small intestines. The lactase breaks down the milk-based sugars into galactose and glucose. These forms of sugar then get absorbed into your bloodstream and used for energy. Symptoms Just because you "}}
