{"latest_judgment":{"docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_10_1464530464#0_2388995264","relevance":3,"reason":"The article is explicitly dedicated to whether adults can suddenly develop lactose intolerance and directly answers that it is possible, with an example of noticing symptoms over time.","learned":"Adults can possibly become lactose intolerant, sometimes noticed over time after consuming milk or ice cream."},"action":{"op":"next","qid":"q167","reason":"The current query is yielding multiple directly relevant documents from varied sources, so continue to retrieve more grade-3 evidence."}}
{"request":{"op":"next","qid":"q167"},"response":{"docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_46_154644860#2_359454272","ok":true,"op":"next","qid":"q167","rank":4,"snippet":"{ \"docid\": \"msmarco_v2.1_doc_46_154644860#2_359454272\" , \"end_char\": 2213.000000 , \"headings\": \"Can <cover>Lactose Intolerance Develop with Age?</cover>Can Lactose Intolerance Develop with Age? Symptoms Other Causes Solutions \" , \"segment\": \"Lactose intolerance develops over time, and the symptoms become much more noticeable as you age. The main symptoms include: Gas Bloating Nausea, often accompanied by vomiting Diarrhea Abdominal cramps Any and all symptoms should be diagnosed by your gastroenterologist for an accurate diagnosis and treatment plan. Lactose intolerance can be difficult to diagnose because its symptoms mimic those of other digestive disorders such as Irritable Bowel Syndrome and GERD. Your Manhattan gastroenterologist may ask you to eliminate milk products for a period of time to see if your symptoms subside. Other tests that can help detect the condition include: Hydrogen breath testing Lactose intolerance testing Other Causes In addition to advancing age, other causes of lactose intolerance can include small intestine injury. Digestive disorders such as Crohn’s disease, an overgrowth of intestinal bacteria, and Celiac disease can lead to lactose intolerance. Any and all symptoms "}}
