{"latest_judgment":{"docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_25_140887620#4_287169326","relevance":3,"reason":"This Mayo Clinic segment from a directly relevant article explains primary lactose intolerance: people start life with normal lactase, lactase production normally decreases, and if it declines below normal at some point, milk products become difficult to digest and symptoms result.","learned":"Primary lactose intolerance can arise over time when lactase production declines below the level needed to digest dairy."},"action":{"op":"next","qid":"q167","reason":"The query continues to retrieve directly relevant evidence, though with some duplicate segments; continue to see whether additional independent grade-3 sources appear."}}
{"request":{"op":"next","qid":"q167"},"response":{"docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_46_154644860#3_359455853","ok":true,"op":"next","qid":"q167","rank":10,"snippet":"{ \"docid\": \"msmarco_v2.1_doc_46_154644860#3_359455853\" , \"end_char\": 2655.000000 , \"headings\": \"Can <cover>Lactose Intolerance Develop with Age?</cover>Can Lactose Intolerance Develop with Age? Symptoms Other Causes Solutions \" , \"segment\": \"Other tests that can help detect the condition include: Hydrogen breath testing Lactose intolerance testing Other Causes In addition to advancing age, other causes of lactose intolerance can include small intestine injury. Digestive disorders such as Crohn’s disease, an overgrowth of intestinal bacteria, and Celiac disease can lead to lactose intolerance. Any and all symptoms should be diagnosed by your gastroenterologist for an accurate diagnosis and treatment plan to exclude any other causes of your symptoms. Your ethnicity also plays a factor. Hispanic, Asian, American Indian and African Americans are more prone to lactose intolerance. Solutions There is no cure for lactose intolerance, though dietary changes can help mitigate your symptoms. Follow your doctor’s orders regarding diet and supplements. You need to make sure you get sufficient calcium if you forgo milk in all its forms, though most adults with lactose intolerance can handle "}}
