{"latest_judgment":{"docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_35_571780126#0_1476414199","relevance":3,"reason":"The article is dedicated to whether lactose intolerance can appear suddenly or develop over time, and it directly states that lactose intolerance is more likely to develop over time with age, though sudden onset can occur after intestinal injury or illness.","learned":"Lactose intolerance usually develops over time with age, but intestinal injury or illness can cause sudden onset."},"action":{"op":"next","qid":"q169","reason":"The exact-phrase query found a directly relevant article; continue in this result set to find more grade-3 documents about lactose intolerance developing over time."}}
{"request":{"op":"next","qid":"q169"},"response":{"docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_21_549512592#1_1155383399","ok":true,"op":"next","qid":"q169","rank":2,"snippet":"{ \"docid\": \"msmarco_v2.1_doc_21_549512592#1_1155383399\" , \"end_char\": 1610.000000 , \"headings\": \"Causes of Intermittent Diarrhea & Gas Causes of Intermittent Diarrhea & Gas<cover>Lactose Intolerance Irritable Bowel Syndrome Celiac Disease \" , \"segment\": \"Some people are deficient in the intestinal enzyme lactase, needed for the breakdown of lactose. This deficiency can lead to bouts of gas and diarrhea. Symptoms of lactase deficiency develop over time, and usually don't appear until adolescence or later. </cover>The cause may have a genetic component, or it can arise after injury to the small intestine from severe intestinal disease, or chemotherapy drugs. The amount and type of milk product that produces symptoms varies greatly from person to person. Symptoms develop after consuming dairy, and may include gas, diarrhea, abdominal pain and nausea. Restriction or avoidance of dairy products relieves symptoms. Lactase supplements are also available, and can help lessen the effects of lactose intolerance. Lactose is a sugar found in milk, and products made from milk. The cause may have a genetic component, or it can arise after injury to the small "}}
