{"request":{"op":"next","qid":"q174"},"response":{"docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_48_471468274#3_816375003","ok":true,"op":"next","qid":"q174","rank":3,"snippet":"{ \"docid\": \"msmarco_v2.1_doc_48_471468274#3_816375003\" , \"end_char\": 2014.000000 , \"headings\": \"Can You Become Lactose Intolerant? Can You Become Lactose Intolerant? What Causes Lactose Intolerance? Who Gets It? Can You <cover>Become Lactose Intolerant Later in Life?</cover>What Should You Do in the Meantime? How to Check If It’s Lactose Intolerance What to Do About Lactose Intolerance How to Deal with Lactose Intolerance \" , \"segment\": \"In which case, it may only be a short term condition. Who Gets It? Lactose intolerance appears to affect both genders equally. Certain ethnic groups tend to be more likely to become lactose intolerant than others. Children are least likely to have issues with lactose. However, many children become lactose intolerant as they edge into adulthood. Many of these children started displaying symptoms in their early teens without realizing it. Can You Become Lactose Intolerant Later in Life? The answer is yes. As lactose moves through the colon it may cause symptoms including pain in the abdomen, gas, bloating and other uncomfortable symptoms.\" , \"start_char\":"}}
