{"latest_judgment":{"docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_48_471468274#3_816375003","relevance":3,"reason":"This is another segment from a dedicated article titled 'Can You Become Lactose Intolerant Later in Life?' and it directly answers 'yes,' explaining that many children become lactose intolerant as they move into adulthood.","learned":"Duplicate/near-duplicate evidence: lactose intolerance can develop later in life, including as children edge into adulthood, and symptoms may begin in the teens."},"action":{"op":"next","qid":"q174","reason":"The later-in-life query is producing directly relevant evidence, so continue to gather more grade-3 results while it remains productive."}}
{"request":{"op":"next","qid":"q174"},"response":{"docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_48_471468274#4_816376265","ok":true,"op":"next","qid":"q174","rank":4,"snippet":"{ \"docid\": \"msmarco_v2.1_doc_48_471468274#4_816376265\" , \"end_char\": 2498.000000 , \"headings\": \"Can You Become Lactose Intolerant? Can You Become Lactose Intolerant? What Causes Lactose Intolerance? Who Gets It? Can You <cover>Become Lactose Intolerant Later in Life?</cover>What Should You Do in the Meantime? How to Check If It’s Lactose Intolerance What to Do About Lactose Intolerance How to Deal with Lactose Intolerance \" , \"segment\": \"However, many children become lactose intolerant as they edge into adulthood. Many of these children started displaying symptoms in their early teens without realizing it. Can You Become Lactose Intolerant Later in Life? The answer is yes. As lactose moves through the colon it may cause symptoms including pain in the abdomen, gas, bloating and other uncomfortable symptoms. For some people, just a swallow of milk may cause these symptoms, for others, it may be an entire glass of milk before they notice any symptoms. Typically, the condition is genetic and will run in the family. However, it's not unusual or unheard of to suddenly develop it when no "}}
