{"latest_judgment":{"docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_48_471468274#4_816376265","relevance":3,"reason":"This is another segment from a dedicated article titled 'Can You Become Lactose Intolerant Later in Life?' and it directly answers yes, noting that many people develop symptoms as they approach adulthood and that sudden development can occur.","learned":"Duplicate/near-duplicate evidence: people can become lactose intolerant later in life; symptoms may start in the teens or adulthood, and sudden development is possible."},"action":{"op":"query","query":"(^ \"suddenly lactose intolerant\" (+ adult adults \"later in life\" develop developed))","reason":"Search for independent articles using the common wording 'suddenly lactose intolerant' to find more pages directly answering whether lactose intolerance can appear after previously tolerating dairy."}}
{"request":{"op":"query","query":"(^ \"suddenly lactose intolerant\" (+ adult adults \"later in life\" develop developed))"},"response":{"docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_09_401510374#19_572979239","ok":true,"op":"query","qid":"q175","rank":1,"snippet":"of GI upset following the consumption of milk does not prove lactose intolerance. So many things can cause random GI upset, it’s very likely the milk was simply coincidental, and something that jumped to your attention because you so seldom drink it. You could be intolerant of other natural dietary sugars (such as those found in broccoli, beans, etc.), or you may have difficulty with certain soluble fibers, like those found in oats. The only way to absolutely diagnose lactose intolerance is a rigid, well-controlled elimination diet and/or medical testing. However. If you are indeed “<cover>suddenly” lactose intolerant, you should know that the vast majority of adults </cover>will gradually acquire some degree of lactase deficiency as they age. This is a natural process, and the degree, frequency and age of onset vary with ethnicity. Nevertheless, the vast majority of the world’s adults have some degree of lactase deficiency.\" , \"start_char\": 8650.000000 , \"title\": \"Lactose Intolerance & Organic Hormone-Free Milk | Serious Eats Talk\" , \"url\": \"http://www.seriouseats.com/talk/2008/10/lactose-intolerance-organic-hormonefree-milk.html\" }"}}
{"request":{"judgments":"29/50"}}
{"latest_judgment":{"docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_09_401510374#19_572979239","relevance":2,"reason":"The Serious Eats Talk result contains direct supporting evidence that adults can gradually acquire lactase deficiency as they age, but it is a forum/talk page and not a document dedicated to answering the medical question.","learned":"Adults can gradually acquire some degree of lactase deficiency as they age, with onset varying by ethnicity, but forum-style results are less useful as evidence."},"action":{"op":"query","query":"(^ \"lactose intolerance\" (+ nhs cleveland webmd healthline medlineplus) (+ develop developed \"later in life\" adult adults age))","reason":"Target recognizable medical/health sources that directly discuss lactose intolerance developing later in life or in adults to find more authoritative grade-3 evidence."}}
{"request":{"op":"query","query":"(^ \"lactose intolerance\" (+ nhs cleveland webmd healthline medlineplus) (+ develop developed \"later in life\" adult adults age))"},"response":{"docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_42_596543092#3_1184243692","ok":true,"op":"query","qid":"q176","rank":1,"snippet":": 2108.000000 , \"headings\": \"Can You Develop Lactose Intolerance? Can You Develop Lactose Intolerance? What is lactose intolerance? Can you develop lactose intolerance? Secondary lactose intolerance Takeaway \" , \"segment\": \"It’s inherited instead of developed. Both parents need the gene mutation to pass it on. Developmental lactose intolerance is typically temporary. It’s found in some babies born prematurely before their small intestine was fully developed. Secondary lactose intolerance isn’t hereditary, but is developed when you have a problem in your small intestine. It can occur at any age. Secondary lactose intolerance Secondary lactose intolerance is caused by a problem in your small intesti ne. If this problem creates a shortage of lactase, then you may develop lactose intolerance. Possible causes of secondary lactose intolerance include: ulcerative colitis gastroenteritis Crohn’s disease celiac disease antibiotics chemotherapy As you get older, your body naturally produces less lactase.\" , \"start_char\": 1323.000000 , \"title\": \"Can You Develop Lactose Intolerance?\" , \"url\": \"https://www.<cover>healthline.com/health/can-you-develop-lactose-intolerance</cover>\" }"}}
{"request":{"judgments":"30/50"}}
{"latest_judgment":{"docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_42_596543092#3_1184243692","relevance":3,"reason":"The Healthline article is explicitly titled 'Can You Develop Lactose Intolerance?' and directly states that secondary lactose intolerance can develop at any age and that the body naturally produces less lactase with age.","learned":"Secondary lactose intolerance can develop at any age due to small-intestine problems, and aging is associated with naturally producing less lactase."},"action":{"op":"next","qid":"q176","reason":"This query targets recognizable medical/health sources and has produced a directly relevant Healthline article, so continue to find additional authoritative grade-3 evidence."}}
{"request":{"op":"next","qid":"q176"},"response":{"docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_42_596543092#0_1184239791","ok":true,"op":"next","qid":"q176","rank":2,"snippet":"Intolerance? Can You Develop Lactose Intolerance? What is lactose intolerance? Can you develop lactose intolerance? Secondary lactose intolerance Takeaway \" , \"segment\": \"Can You Develop Lactose Intolerance? Can You Develop Lactose Intolerance? Medically reviewed by Katherine Marengo LDN, R.D. — Written by Scott Frothingham on January 9, 2019 Overview Developing lactose intolerance Secondary lactose intolerance Takeaway Share on Pinterest What is lactose intolerance? If you have lactose intolerance, it means you’re unable to fully digest the lactose in milk. For people with lactose intolerance, drinking milk or eating dairy products can result in: abdominal cramps nausea gas bloating diarrhea Lactose intolerance — also referred to as lactose malabsorption — is usually caused by having too little of an enzyme produced in your small intestine called lactase. Can you develop lactose intolerance? Lactose intolerance can be developed at any age. There are four main types: primary congenital developmental secondary Primary and congenital lactose intolerance are both inherited.\" , \"start_char\": 0.000000 , \"title\": \"Can You Develop Lactose Intolerance?\" , \"url\": \"https://www.<cover>healthline.com/health/can-you-develop-lactose-intolerance</cover>\" }"}}
{"request":{"judgments":"31/50"}}
{"latest_judgment":{"docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_42_596543092#0_1184239791","relevance":3,"reason":"The Healthline article is dedicated to the question 'Can You Develop Lactose Intolerance?' and directly states that lactose intolerance can be developed at any age.","learned":"Lactose intolerance can develop at any age; Healthline distinguishes inherited primary/congenital forms from developmental and secondary types."},"action":{"op":"next","qid":"q176","reason":"The targeted medical-source query is producing directly relevant evidence, so continue to look for more authoritative grade-3 results."}}
{"request":{"op":"next","qid":"q176"},"response":{"docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_42_596543092#2_1184242476","ok":true,"op":"next","qid":"q176","rank":3,"snippet":"1675.000000 , \"headings\": \"Can You Develop Lactose Intolerance? Can You Develop Lactose Intolerance? What is lactose intolerance? Can you develop lactose intolerance? Secondary lactose intolerance Takeaway \" , \"segment\": \"Primary lactose intolerance is the most common. Your lactase production starts to decrease as you age and you become less dependent on dairy, usually after the age of 2. You may not notice symptoms, however, until you’re an adult. It may seem like lactose intolerance has developed, but primary lactose intolerance is hereditary. Congenital lactose intolerance is a rare condition found in newborn babies. It’s inherited instead of developed. Both parents need the gene mutation to pass it on. Developmental lactose intolerance is typically temporary. It’s found in some babies born prematurely before their small intestine was fully developed. Secondary lactose intolerance isn’t hereditary, but is developed when you have a problem in your small intestine.\" , \"start_char\": 916.000000 , \"title\": \"Can You Develop Lactose Intolerance?\" , \"url\": \"https://www.<cover>healthline.com/health/can-you-develop-lactose-intolerance</cover>\" }"}}
{"request":{"judgments":"32/50"}}
{"latest_judgment":{"docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_42_596543092#2_1184242476","relevance":3,"reason":"This is another segment from the Healthline article dedicated to 'Can You Develop Lactose Intolerance?' and it directly explains that lactase production decreases with age, symptoms may not appear until adulthood, and secondary lactose intolerance can develop after small-intestine problems.","learned":"Duplicate/near-duplicate evidence: lactase production can decrease with age, adult symptoms may appear later, and secondary lactose intolerance can develop due to small-intestine problems."},"action":{"op":"query","query":"(^ \"lactose intolerance\" (+ \"cleveland clinic\" cleveland) (+ develop developed adult adults age later))","reason":"Search specifically for Cleveland Clinic or similarly authoritative medical evidence about lactose intolerance developing in adulthood or with age, to add independent grade-3 sources."}}
{"request":{"op":"query","query":"(^ \"lactose intolerance\" (+ \"cleveland clinic\" cleveland) (+ develop developed adult adults age later))"},"response":{"docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_06_1427301721#1_1993087412","ok":true,"op":"query","qid":"q177","rank":1,"snippet":"a lactose-free diet and lifestyle \" , \"segment\": \"Lactose is commonly found in dairy products, such as milk and yogurt. You become lactose intolerant when your small intestine stops making enough of the enzyme lactase to digest and break down the lactose. When this happens, the undigested lactose moves into the large intestine. The bacteria that are normally present in your large intestine interact with the undigested lactose and cause symptoms such as bloating, gas, and diarrhea. The condition may also be called lactase deficiency. <cover>Lactose intolerance is very common in adults, particularly those with Asian, African, and Hispanic ancestry. According to the Cleveland </cover>Clinic, more than 30 million American people are lactose intolerant. The condition isn’t serious but may be unpleasant. Lactose intolerance usually causes gastrointestinal symptoms, such as gas, bloating, and diarrhea, about 30 minutes to two hours after ingesting milk or other dairy products containing lactose. People who are lactose intolerant may need to avoid eating these products or take medications containing the lactase enzyme before doing so.\" , \"start_char\": 501.000000 , \"title\": \"Lactose Intolerance: Types, Causes, and Treatment"}}
{"request":{"judgments":"33/50"}}
{"latest_judgment":{"docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_06_1427301721#1_1993087412","relevance":2,"reason":"The document is generally about lactose intolerance types, causes, and treatment, and it explains that you become lactose intolerant when the small intestine stops making enough lactase, but the visible snippet is not specifically dedicated to whether this can develop over time or later in life.","learned":"Lactose intolerance occurs when the small intestine no longer makes enough lactase to digest lactose and is common in adults."},"action":{"op":"query","query":"(^ \"lactose intolerance\" (+ \"develop at any age\" \"can develop at any age\" \"develop later in life\") (+ mayo nhs cleveland webmd medlineplus))","reason":"Search for authoritative medical pages that directly state lactose intolerance can develop at any age or later in life, which should yield more dedicated grade-3 evidence."}}
{"request":{"op":"query","query":"(^ \"lactose intolerance\" (+ \"develop at any age\" \"can develop at any age\" \"develop later in life\") (+ mayo nhs cleveland webmd medlineplus))"},"response":{"docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_25_140887620#5_287170842","ok":true,"op":"next","qid":"q178","rank":4,"snippet":"{ \"docid\": \"msmarco_v2.1_doc_25_140887620#5_287170842\" , \"end_char\": 3137.000000 , \"headings\": \"Mayo Clinic Q and A: <cover>Lactose Intolerance Can Develop at Any Age Mayo </cover>Clinic Q and A: Lactose Intolerance Can Develop at Any Age New SW Region VP for Mayo Clinic Health System In the Loop: Tips for Things Children Swallow \" , \"segment\": \"The low amount of lactase then makes milk products difficult to digest and leads to lactose intolerance symptoms. Your doctor can confirm a diagnosis of lactose intolerance with a clinical test. One that’s often used is a lactose tolerance test. It assesses your body’s reaction to a dose of lactose. After you consume a drink containing lactose, a sample of your blood is taken to measure glucose levels. If your glucose level does not rise, it means your body isn’t properly digesting and absorbing the lactose. Alternatively, another test called the hydrogen breath test may be used. This test also requires you to consume a drink that contains high levels of lactose. Your doctor next measures the amount ","skipped":[{"docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_25_140887620#0_287163141","rank":1,"relevance":3},{"docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_25_140887620#1_287164453","rank":2,"relevance":3},{"docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_25_140887620#4_287169326","rank":3,"relevance":3}]}}
